## 1. Strongest new result

Under an explicit supplied-factor, fixed-cut, source-discarded, **cumulative-budget destructive-update** contract, there is a coordinate-aware persistent state that supports exact residual model counts after every legal restriction prefix without rescanning the source factors.

For row profiles \(a\), store low-degree profile count moments
\[
A_a(T)=\sum_{x:u_x=a} \prod_{i\in T}x_i
\]
and matching column profile-character moments
\[
B_a(T)=\sum_y(-1)^{a\cdot w_y}\prod_{j\in T}y_j,
\]
through the current remaining horizon. A restriction \(z=b\) updates moments by the exact two-term rule
\[
F'(T)=F(T\cup\{z\})\quad(b=1),\qquad
F'(T)=F(T)-F(T\cup\{z\})\quad(b=0).
\]
The exact residual count is recovered in \(O(s)\le O(2^r)\) integer multiply-adds from the zero-degree moments.

## 2. Exact theorem / resource statement

Let \(s\) be the number of occurring nonzero profiles on the chosen anchor side and
\[
D(d,h)=\sum_{j=0}^{\min(d,h)}\binom dj.
\]
For the row-anchored fixed-width state, initial sparse storage is
\[
S_0\le s\bigl[r+(p+1)D(p,k)+(q+2)D(q,k)\bigr]+O(n+k+r)\text{ bits},
\]
with dense worst case obtained by \(s=2^r-1\) and no stored profile labels. An update on an affected side with \(d\) free coordinates and remaining horizon \(h\) uses
\[
U=sD(d-1,h-1)
\]
exact copy/subtract operations. A count query uses \(T=O(s)\) exact integer multiply-adds. One direct construction has cost
\[
O\!\left(r(2^p+2^q)+2^pD(p,k)+2^qD(q,k)+r2^rD(q,k)\right).
\]
The column-anchored theorem is symmetric.

